  "review_note": "Derived on 2026-10-13 by reading the vendored 3.1.0 sources (call sites, env wiring, compose depends_on), independently of gira output. Evidence rule: a runtime call site or env wiring when the caller's source is vendored; compose depends_on only when the caller's source is not vendored and nothing better exists. Re-checked on 2026-10-13 against the full upstream tree at upstream_sha (GIRA_EVAL_FULL_CORPUS=1): every anchor resolves, the vendored snapshot is byte-identical to upstream, and every expected id names a Component or proto/topic Contract that exists there. Not yet reviewed by a human; thresholds are reported, not enforced (spec part C, gate semantics). Blind re-derivation on 2026-10-13: three subagents re-derived all 12 Impact Sets from the full tree at upstream_sha without seeing this file; 6 tasks matched exactly. Corrections decided by the owner (2026-10-13, \"sim\"): task-02 adds service:agent downstream; task-07 drops service:agent downstream and adds service:opamp-server upstream; task-11 replaces service:product-catalog with service:frontend upstream; task-05/06 add the broker service:kafka upstream; task-01 keeps the topic consumers downstream; task-11 keeps env-gated service:mcp.",
